# structural gaps (cycle 0, untiered records, no rollup/escalation/spend/
# inspect_modes). It stands in for the real archive because
# foundry-archive/ is git-ignored and this command is re-executed inside a
# 'git worktree add --detach' checkout, which holds tracked files only.
# The real archive is asserted by the skipif-guarded
# test_thunder_viper_prints_the_baseline_beside_the_current_run.
#
# Every column the archive cannot supply is null -- never 0, and never a
# failure token. Exit 0: a pre-release archive is not a failure.
#
# GRIND cycle 2, D-022 / D-036: `cycles` is now derived by
# foundry_state.derive_cycle_count -- ONE derivation, called by this command
# and by foundry_report -- and it consults the DEFECT LEDGER as well as the
# counter and the roll-up. That is what rescues an archive whose counter never
# moved: this fixture's records span cycles 0-5, so it reports six cycles
# rather than the one its stale counter alone would give. On the real
# thunder-viper archive the same derivation reproduces the published 22, and
# `meets_target.grind_cycles` there is FALSE -- the tool no longer certifies
# the run whose 22 cycles are the reason the target exists.

